                        "sense_id": "04c29738-8a71-34bc-9567-0a51d0153d78",
                        "entry_id": "64eba6b8-2755-30e6-b2c0-d9dc40630a45",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A formal solemn objection or other declaration."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b2dcf57-8e6c-4f63-9ee9-53af41167159",
                                "sense_id": "04c29738-8a71-34bc-9567-0a51d0153d78",
                                "text": "October 28, 1552, Hugh Latimer, Sermon on the Gospel for St Simon and St Jude's Day\nThe protestation of our faith."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1cbffc4-a2f4-458d-9200-dc579cb744f8",
                                "sense_id": "04c29738-8a71-34bc-9567-0a51d0153d78",
                                "text": "“These are but words, young man,” answered Glendinning, “large protestations are often used to supply the place of effectual service.[…]”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc973fc0-3766-490f-8cbb-5a6b5024b13f",
                                "sense_id": "04c29738-8a71-34bc-9567-0a51d0153d78",
                                "text": "Mechanically he retained the hand that trembled in his own—but Isabella needed no protestations—one word from his mouth had been enough, and she sat in silent \"measureless content.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa3e7e29-a782-3167-adaa-cc81bbc928b3",
                        "entry_id": "64eba6b8-2755-30e6-b2c0-d9dc40630a45",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A declaration in common-law pleading, by which the party interposes an oblique allegation or denial of some fact, protesting that it does or does not exist, and at the same time avoiding a direct affirmation or denial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "historical",
                            "uncountable"
